const timeData={
  concept:['Packet switching foundations','Researchers proposed that messages should be divided into small packets so many users could share a network efficiently. This became a key foundation for modern data communication and the Internet.','Packet switching foundations','Early ideas showed that data could be broken into packets and shared across communication links more efficiently.','Send data as packets, not one dedicated circuit.','Efficient sharing and resilience became possible.','Today’s IP networks still move information as packets.','This concept made large-scale internetworking practical.'],
  arpa:['ARPANET','In 1969, ARPANET connected research institutions and demonstrated remote computer communication across packet-switched links. It showed that networked computers could share resources over distance.','ARPANET research network','ARPANET connected research institutions and demonstrated packet-switched networking in practice.','Connect distant institutions through a shared research network.','It proved that large-scale networking could work in practice.','Remote login and resource sharing between institutions.','It is a major early milestone in Internet history.'],
  email:['E-mail','In the early 1970s, e-mail became one of the first widely used network applications. It showed that networking was valuable for person-to-person communication, not only machine access.','E-mail as an early network application','E-mail showed that networks were useful for human communication, not only machine access.','Exchange messages electronically across a network.','It gave people a practical reason to use networks regularly.','Users send digital messages between accounts and systems.','Applications helped transform infrastructure into daily usefulness.'],
  tcp:['TCP/IP and DNS','In 1983, TCP/IP became the standard protocol suite for internetworking, and DNS followed to make names easier to use. Together they helped separate networks communicate as one Internet.','TCP/IP and DNS standards','Common protocols and naming helped separate networks communicate as one Internet.','Use shared protocols for addressing, routing, and delivery.','Standards made the Internet scalable and interoperable.','DNS maps human-friendly names to IP addresses.','Without shared standards, separate networks remain isolated.'],
  www:['World Wide Web','Between 1989 and the early 1990s, the Web introduced pages, hyperlinks, browsers, URLs, and web servers. It made the Internet much easier for ordinary users to access and understand.','World Wide Web','Web pages, hyperlinks, browsers, URLs, and HTTP made the Internet easier for ordinary users.','Use browsers to open pages linked by URLs and hyperlinks.','It expanded Internet use far beyond specialists.','HTML, HTTP, URLs, web browsers, and websites.','The Web changed the Internet into a mass public medium.'],
  broadband:['Commercial Internet and broadband','In the late 1990s and 2000s, Internet access spread to homes and businesses through ISPs and broadband connections. Search engines, online shopping, and digital media became common.','Commercial Internet and broadband','ISPs and broadband access brought faster Internet into homes, schools, and businesses.','Provide faster and more convenient access through ISPs.','The Internet became mainstream for work, study, and entertainment.','Search, e-commerce, media, and online services grew rapidly.','Faster access changed user behavior and expectations.'],
  mobile:['Mobile, Wi‑Fi, and cloud','In the 2000s and 2010s, wireless networking and smartphones made Internet access portable, while cloud computing moved storage and applications into large data centers.','Mobile, Wi‑Fi, and cloud','Smartphones, Wi‑Fi, and cloud platforms made Internet access portable and service-based.','Access the Internet through Wi‑Fi, mobile networks, and cloud services.','Internet use became continuous and location-independent.','Apps, online storage, collaboration tools, and cloud platforms.','The network became the platform for modern digital life.'],
  ai:['IoT, streaming, and AI services','Today the Internet connects smart devices, sensors, streaming platforms, cloud APIs, and AI services. Modern applications depend on high-speed, large-scale networks and data centers.','Connected devices and AI services','Modern Internet services depend on cloud platforms, data centers, streaming traffic, IoT, and AI services.','Connect users, devices, services, and intelligent systems.','The Internet is now a service ecosystem, not just a communication link.','IoT, streaming, cloud applications, and AI tools.','Modern services combine networking with computing and data at scale.']
};

